-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/560223d0-2ba0-4b00-a44c-70601094842f
-- title:
--   §3, pp. 9–10 — the COMDP (ℙ(𝕏), 𝔸, q, c̄), its optimal values, the sets A_{t,α}, A_α, statements (i)–(vi) of Theorem 3.1, and the partition conditions of Theorem 7.1
-- statement:
--   The completely observable MDP (COMDP) of a POMDP and the objects in which its optimality properties are stated.
--
--   1. **Belief space.** $\mathbb P(\mathbb X)$ with the topology of weak convergence and its Borel σ-algebra $\mathcal B(\mathbb P(\mathbb X))$.
--   2. **The COMDP** $(\mathbb P(\mathbb X),\mathbb A,q,\bar c)$ (p. 9): the MDP with state space $\mathbb P(\mathbb X)$, action set $\mathbb A$, transition probability $q(dz'|z,a)$ of (3.5) built from a filter $H$ satisfying (3.3), and one-step cost $\bar c(z,a)=\int_{\mathbb X}c(x,a)\,z(dx)$ (3.8). Its policies are the I-policies on information vectors $i_t=(z_0,a_0,\dots,z_t)$; write $\bar v_{t,\alpha}$, $\bar v_\alpha$ for its optimal values.
--   3. **Bellman expressions.** $\bar c(z,a)+\alpha\int_{\mathbb P(\mathbb X)}v(z')\,q(dz'|z,a)$ and its expanded form
--   $$\int_{\mathbb X}c(x,a)z(dx)+\alpha\int_{\mathbb X}\int_{\mathbb X}\int_{\mathbb Y}v(H(z,a,y))\,Q(dy|a,x')P(dx'|x,a)z(dx).$$
--   4. **Minimizer sets.** $A_{t,\alpha}(z)=\{a:\bar v_{t+1,\alpha}(z)=\bar c(z,a)+\alpha\int\bar v_{t,\alpha}\,dq(\cdot|z,a)\}$ and $A_\alpha(z)=\{a:\bar v_\alpha(z)=\bar c(z,a)+\alpha\int\bar v_\alpha\,dq(\cdot|z,a)\}$.
--   5. **Statements (i)–(vi) of Theorem 3.1** as one proposition: lower semicontinuity and convergence of the values, the optimality equations (3.10), (3.11) with attained minima, nonemptiness, Borel graphs and compactness of the minimizer sets, optimal Markov and stationary I-policies, and inf-compactness of the values when $\bar c$ is inf-compact.
--   6. **Partition conditions (Theorem 7.1).** For $\mathbb Y_2\subseteq\mathbb Y$: setwise continuity of $R'(\cdot|z,a)$ restricted to Borel subsets of $\mathbb Y_2$, and Assumption (H) on $\mathbb Y_2$ — a subsequence and a Borel $C\subseteq\mathbb Y_2$ with $R'(\mathbb Y_2\setminus C|z,a)=0$ along which $H(z^{(n_k)},a^{(n_k)},y)\to H(z,a,y)$ weakly for every $y\in C$.
--
--   These are the shared objects of Theorems 3.1, 3.2, 7.1 and 8.2.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The POMDP cost is $c=\ell+f$ with $\ell\in\mathbb R$ and $f\ge0$, so $\bar c=\ell+\int f(\cdot,a)\,dz$. Mathlib's default σ-algebra on probability measures is the one generated by $\mu\mapsto\mu(B)$; the COMDP uses the Borel σ-algebra of the weak topology instead, as the paper does. The COMDP kernel is $q$ whenever $(z,a)\mapsto q(\cdot|z,a)$ is a measurable family of probability measures, which holds for every filter; otherwise a placeholder identity kernel is used, which never occurs for a filter. The restricted observation law is not renormalized and may have mass zero.
-- source:
--   Feinberg, Kasyanov, Zgurovsky, Partially Observable Total-Cost Markov Decision Processes with Weakly Continuous Transition Probabilities, arXiv:1401.2168v2, §3, COMDP and (3.8), p. 9; Theorem 3.1 (i)–(vi), (3.10), (3.11), p. 10; Theorem 7.1 (b), (c)(ii), p. 25

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_FeinbergLiang_ACOE_MDP
import Definitions.Def_FeinbergPOMDP_WStar_Model
import Definitions.Def_FeinbergPOMDP_WStar_Supplement_MDPValues

open scoped ENNReal NNReal Topology
open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter FeinbergLiang.ACOE FeinbergPOMDP.WStar

namespace FeinbergPOMDP.WStar.Supplement

/-! Feinberg, Kasyanov, Zgurovsky, *Partially Observable Total-Cost Markov Decision Processes with
Weakly Continuous Transition Probabilities*, arXiv:1401.2168v2, §3, pp. 9–10: the COMDP
`(ℙ(𝕏), 𝔸, q, c̄)` as an MDP, its expected costs and optimal values `v̄_{t,α}`, `v̄_α` over all
I-policies, the sets `A_{t,α}(z)`, `A_α(z)` and the conclusions (i)–(vi) of Theorem 3.1; and the
two conditions on a partition `𝕐 = 𝕐₁ ∪ 𝕐₂` used in Theorem 7.1 (p. 25). -/

/-- The belief space `ℙ(𝕏)` with the topology of weak convergence and **its Borel σ-algebra**
`ℬ(ℙ(𝕏))` (the σ-algebra the paper uses on `ℙ(𝕏)`; Mathlib's default instance on
`ProbabilityMeasure X` is the one generated by `μ ↦ μ(B)` instead). -/
def Belief (X : Type*) [MeasurableSpace X] : Type _ := ProbabilityMeasure X

section Belief

variable {X : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X] [MeasurableSpace X] [OpensMeasurableSpace X]

noncomputable instance : TopologicalSpace (Belief X) :=
  inferInstanceAs (TopologicalSpace (ProbabilityMeasure X))

noncomputable instance : MeasurableSpace (Belief X) := borel (Belief X)

instance : BorelSpace (Belief X) := ⟨rfl⟩

/-- A belief `z ∈ ℙ(𝕏)` as a probability measure on `𝕏`. -/
def Belief.toPM (z : Belief X) : ProbabilityMeasure X := z

end Belief

section COMDP

variable {X Y A : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X] [MeasurableSpace X] [OpensMeasurableSpace X]
  [MeasurableSpace Y] [MeasurableSpace A]

/-- The transition probability `q(dz′ | z, a)` of (3.5) packaged as a stochastic kernel on
`ℙ(𝕏)` given `ℙ(𝕏) × 𝔸`.

Formalization Note. For a filter `H` satisfying (3.3) (`IsFilter`, which includes joint Borel
measurability of `H`), `(z, a) ↦ q(· | z, a) = beliefTransition P Q H z a` is a measurable family of
probability measures, as the paper states on p. 8; the first branch is then taken and the kernel is
exactly `q`. The second branch (the identity kernel) only makes the definition total and is never
used for a filter. -/
noncomputable def comdpKernel [TopologicalSpace A]
    (P : Kernel (X × A) X) [IsMarkovKernel P] (Q : Kernel (A × X) Y) [IsMarkovKernel Q]
    (H : ProbabilityMeasure X → A → Y → ProbabilityMeasure X) : Kernel (Belief X × A) (Belief X) :=
  open Classical in
  if h : Measurable (fun p : Belief X × A => (beliefTransition P Q H p.1 p.2 : Measure (Belief X))) ∧
      ∀ p : Belief X × A, IsProbabilityMeasure (beliefTransition P Q H p.1 p.2 : Measure (Belief X))
  then ⟨fun p => beliefTransition P Q H p.1 p.2, h.1⟩
  else Kernel.deterministic Prod.fst measurable_fst

instance [TopologicalSpace A]
    (P : Kernel (X × A) X) [IsMarkovKernel P] (Q : Kernel (A × X) Y) [IsMarkovKernel Q]
    (H : ProbabilityMeasure X → A → Y → ProbabilityMeasure X) :
    IsMarkovKernel (comdpKernel P Q H) := by
  unfold comdpKernel
  split_ifs with h
  · exact ⟨fun p => h.2 p⟩
  · infer_instance

/-- The COMDP `(ℙ(𝕏), 𝔸, q, c̄)` (p. 9) as an MDP: state space `ℙ(𝕏)`, action set `𝔸`, transition
probability `q` of (3.5) and one-step cost `c̄(z, a) = ∫ c(x, a) z(dx) = lower + beliefCost f z a`
(3.8), where the POMDP cost is `c(x, a) = lower + f x a`. Its policies are the I-policies (p. 9):
randomized, history-dependent decision rules on the information vectors
`i_t = (z₀, a₀, …, z_{t−1}, a_{t−1}, z_t)`. -/
noncomputable def COMDP [TopologicalSpace A]
    (P : Kernel (X × A) X) [IsMarkovKernel P] (Q : Kernel (A × X) Y) [IsMarkovKernel Q]
    (H : ProbabilityMeasure X → A → Y → ProbabilityMeasure X) (lower : ℝ) (f : X → A → ℝ≥0∞) :
    MDP (Belief X) A where
  lower := lower
  cost := beliefCost f
  q := comdpKernel P Q H

/-- The expression minimized in the first line of (3.10)–(3.11):
`c̄(z, a) + α ∫_{ℙ(𝕏)} v(z′) q(dz′ | z, a)`. -/
noncomputable def bellmanRHS [TopologicalSpace A]
    (P : Kernel (X × A) X) [IsMarkovKernel P] (Q : Kernel (A × X) Y) [IsMarkovKernel Q]
    (H : ProbabilityMeasure X → A → Y → ProbabilityMeasure X) (lower : ℝ) (f : X → A → ℝ≥0∞)
    (α : ℝ) (v : Belief X → EReal) (z : Belief X) (a : A) : EReal :=
  ((lower : EReal) + (beliefCost f z a : EReal)) +
    (α : EReal) * lintegralE (S := Belief X) (beliefTransition P Q H z a) v

/-- The expression minimized in the second line of (3.10)–(3.11):
`∫_𝕏 c(x, a) z(dx) + α ∫_𝕏 ∫_𝕏 ∫_𝕐 v(H(z, a, y)) Q(dy | a, x′) P(dx′ | x, a) z(dx)`, with the
triple integral of the extended-real `v` taken as positive part minus negative part. -/
noncomputable def expandedRHS
    (P : Kernel (X × A) X) [IsMarkovKernel P] (Q : Kernel (A × X) Y) [IsMarkovKernel Q]
    (H : ProbabilityMeasure X → A → Y → ProbabilityMeasure X) (lower : ℝ) (f : X → A → ℝ≥0∞)
    (α : ℝ) (v : Belief X → EReal) (z : Belief X) (a : A) : EReal :=
  ((lower : EReal) + ((∫⁻ x, f x a ∂((Belief.toPM z : ProbabilityMeasure X) : Measure X) : ℝ≥0∞) : EReal)) +
    (α : EReal) *
      (((∫⁻ x, ∫⁻ x', ∫⁻ y, (v (H z a y)).toENNReal ∂(Q (a, x')) ∂(P (x, a))
          ∂((Belief.toPM z : ProbabilityMeasure X) : Measure X) : ℝ≥0∞) : EReal) -
       ((∫⁻ x, ∫⁻ x', ∫⁻ y, (-(v (H z a y))).toENNReal ∂(Q (a, x')) ∂(P (x, a))
          ∂((Belief.toPM z : ProbabilityMeasure X) : Measure X) : ℝ≥0∞) : EReal))

/-- The sets `A_{t,α}(z) = {a ∈ 𝔸 : v̄_{t+1,α}(z) = c̄(z, a) + α ∫ v̄_{t,α}(z′) q(dz′ | z, a)}`
of Theorem 3.1(ii). -/
def optActionsT [TopologicalSpace A]
    (P : Kernel (X × A) X) [IsMarkovKernel P] (Q : Kernel (A × X) Y) [IsMarkovKernel Q]
    (H : ProbabilityMeasure X → A → Y → ProbabilityMeasure X) (lower : ℝ) (f : X → A → ℝ≥0∞)
    (α : ℝ) (t : ℕ) (z : Belief X) : Set A :=
  {a | optHorizonCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) (t + 1) α z =
    bellmanRHS P Q H lower f α (optHorizonCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) t α) z a}

/-- The sets `A_α(z) = {a ∈ 𝔸 : v̄_α(z) = c̄(z, a) + α ∫ v̄_α(z′) q(dz′ | z, a)}` of
Theorem 3.1(iv). -/
def optActions [TopologicalSpace A]
    (P : Kernel (X × A) X) [IsMarkovKernel P] (Q : Kernel (A × X) Y) [IsMarkovKernel Q]
    (H : ProbabilityMeasure X → A → Y → ProbabilityMeasure X) (lower : ℝ) (f : X → A → ℝ≥0∞)
    (α : ℝ) (z : Belief X) : Set A :=
  {a | optDiscountedCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) α z =
    bellmanRHS P Q H lower f α (optDiscountedCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) α) z a}

/-- Statements (i)–(vi) of Theorem 3.1 (p. 10) for the COMDP `(ℙ(𝕏), 𝔸, q, c̄)` built from the
filter `H`, the cost `c = lower + f` and the discount factor `α`. Write `v̄_{t,α}` for
`optHorizonCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) t α` and `v̄_α` for `optDiscountedCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) α`;
"`v = min_a g(a)`" is written as "some `a₀` has `v = g(a₀)` and `v ≤ g(a)` for all `a`". -/
structure COMDPOptimality [TopologicalSpace A]
    (P : Kernel (X × A) X) [IsMarkovKernel P] (Q : Kernel (A × X) Y) [IsMarkovKernel Q]
    (H : ProbabilityMeasure X → A → Y → ProbabilityMeasure X) (lower : ℝ) (f : X → A → ℝ≥0∞)
    (α : ℝ) : Prop where
  /-- (i) `v̄_{t,α}`, `t = 0, 1, …`, is lower semi-continuous on `ℙ(𝕏)`. -/
  lsc_horizon : ∀ t : ℕ, LowerSemicontinuous (optHorizonCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) t α)
  /-- (i) `v̄_α` is lower semi-continuous on `ℙ(𝕏)`. -/
  lsc_discounted : LowerSemicontinuous (optDiscountedCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) α)
  /-- (i) `v̄_{t,α}(z) → v̄_α(z)` as `t → ∞` for all `z`. -/
  tendsto_value : ∀ z : Belief X,
    Tendsto (fun t : ℕ => optHorizonCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) t α z) atTop
      (𝓝 (optDiscountedCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) α z))
  /-- (ii) first line of (3.10): `v̄_{t+1,α}(z) = min_a {c̄(z, a) + α ∫ v̄_{t,α} dq(· | z, a)}`. -/
  bellman_horizon : ∀ (t : ℕ) (z : Belief X),
    (∃ a₀ : A, optHorizonCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) (t + 1) α z =
        bellmanRHS P Q H lower f α (optHorizonCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) t α) z a₀) ∧
    ∀ a : A, optHorizonCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) (t + 1) α z ≤
        bellmanRHS P Q H lower f α (optHorizonCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) t α) z a
  /-- (ii) second line of (3.10): the same value is the minimum of the expanded expression. -/
  bellman_horizon_expanded : ∀ (t : ℕ) (z : Belief X),
    (∃ a₀ : A, optHorizonCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) (t + 1) α z =
        expandedRHS P Q H lower f α (optHorizonCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) t α) z a₀) ∧
    ∀ a : A, optHorizonCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) (t + 1) α z ≤
        expandedRHS P Q H lower f α (optHorizonCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) t α) z a
  /-- (ii) `v̄_{0,α} = 0`. -/
  value_zero : ∀ z : Belief X, optHorizonCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) 0 α z = 0
  /-- (ii) the sets `A_{t,α}(z)` are nonempty. -/
  optActionsT_nonempty : ∀ (t : ℕ) (z : Belief X), (optActionsT P Q H lower f α t z).Nonempty
  /-- (ii)(a) the graph `Gr(A_{t,α})` is a Borel subset of `ℙ(𝕏) × 𝔸`. -/
  optActionsT_graph : ∀ t : ℕ,
    MeasurableSet {p : Belief X × A | p.2 ∈ optActionsT P Q H lower f α t p.1}
  /-- (ii)(b) if `v̄_{t+1,α}(z) = +∞` then `A_{t,α}(z) = 𝔸`. -/
  optActionsT_top : ∀ (t : ℕ) (z : Belief X),
    optHorizonCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) (t + 1) α z = ⊤ → optActionsT P Q H lower f α t z = Set.univ
  /-- (ii)(b) if `v̄_{t+1,α}(z) < +∞` then `A_{t,α}(z)` is compact. -/
  optActionsT_compact : ∀ (t : ℕ) (z : Belief X),
    optHorizonCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) (t + 1) α z < ⊤ → IsCompact (optActionsT P Q H lower f α t z)
  /-- (iii) for each `T ≥ 1` there is an optimal Markov `T`-horizon I-policy. -/
  markov_exists : ∀ T : ℕ, 1 ≤ T → ∃ (φ : ℕ → Belief X → A) (hφ : ∀ t, Measurable (φ t)),
    IsHorizonOptimal (COMDP P Q H lower f) (markovPolicy φ hφ) T α
  /-- (iii) a Markov `T`-horizon I-policy with `φ_{T−1−t}(z) ∈ A_{t,α}(z)` for all `z` and
  `t = 0, …, T − 1` is `T`-horizon optimal. -/
  markov_of_mem : ∀ T : ℕ, 1 ≤ T → ∀ (φ : ℕ → Belief X → A) (hφ : ∀ t, Measurable (φ t)),
    (∀ t, t < T → ∀ z, φ (T - 1 - t) z ∈ optActionsT P Q H lower f α t z) →
      IsHorizonOptimal (COMDP P Q H lower f) (markovPolicy φ hφ) T α
  /-- (iv) first line of (3.11): `v̄_α(z) = min_a {c̄(z, a) + α ∫ v̄_α dq(· | z, a)}`. -/
  bellman_discounted : ∀ z : Belief X,
    (∃ a₀ : A, optDiscountedCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) α z =
        bellmanRHS P Q H lower f α (optDiscountedCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) α) z a₀) ∧
    ∀ a : A, optDiscountedCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) α z ≤
        bellmanRHS P Q H lower f α (optDiscountedCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) α) z a
  /-- (iv) second line of (3.11). -/
  bellman_discounted_expanded : ∀ z : Belief X,
    (∃ a₀ : A, optDiscountedCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) α z =
        expandedRHS P Q H lower f α (optDiscountedCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) α) z a₀) ∧
    ∀ a : A, optDiscountedCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) α z ≤
        expandedRHS P Q H lower f α (optDiscountedCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) α) z a
  /-- (iv) the sets `A_α(z)` are nonempty. -/
  optActions_nonempty : ∀ z : Belief X, (optActions P Q H lower f α z).Nonempty
  /-- (iv)(a) the graph `Gr(A_α)` is a Borel subset of `ℙ(𝕏) × 𝔸`. -/
  optActions_graph : MeasurableSet {p : Belief X × A | p.2 ∈ optActions P Q H lower f α p.1}
  /-- (iv)(b) if `v̄_α(z) = +∞` then `A_α(z) = 𝔸`. -/
  optActions_top : ∀ z : Belief X,
    optDiscountedCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) α z = ⊤ → optActions P Q H lower f α z = Set.univ
  /-- (iv)(b) if `v̄_α(z) < +∞` then `A_α(z)` is compact. -/
  optActions_compact : ∀ z : Belief X,
    optDiscountedCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) α z < ⊤ → IsCompact (optActions P Q H lower f α z)
  /-- (v) there is a stationary discount-optimal I-policy. -/
  stationary_exists : ∃ (φ : Belief X → A) (hφ : Measurable φ),
    IsDiscountOptimal (COMDP P Q H lower f) (Policy.ofStationary φ hφ) α
  /-- (v) a stationary I-policy `φ` is optimal iff `φ(z) ∈ A_α(z)` for all `z`. -/
  stationary_iff : ∀ (φ : Belief X → A) (hφ : Measurable φ),
    IsDiscountOptimal (COMDP P Q H lower f) (Policy.ofStationary φ hφ) α ↔
      ∀ z, φ z ∈ optActions P Q H lower f α z
  /-- (vi) if `c̄` is inf-compact on `ℙ(𝕏) × 𝔸`, then `v̄_{t,α}`, `t = 1, 2, …`, and `v̄_α` are
  inf-compact on `ℙ(𝕏)`. -/
  infCompact_values :
    InfCompact (fun p : Belief X × A => (lower : EReal) + (beliefCost f p.1 p.2 : EReal)) →
      (∀ t : ℕ, 1 ≤ t → InfCompact (optHorizonCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) t α)) ∧
      InfCompact (optDiscountedCost (COMDP P Q H lower f) α)

end COMDP

section Partition

variable {X Y A : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X] [MeasurableSpace X] [OpensMeasurableSpace X]
  [MeasurableSpace Y] [MeasurableSpace A] [TopologicalSpace A]

/-- Condition (b) of Theorem 7.1 (p. 25): the restriction of `R′(· | z, a)` to `(𝕐₂, ℬ(𝕐₂))` is
setwise continuous in `(z, a)`: for every sequence `(z⁽ⁿ⁾, a⁽ⁿ⁾) → (z, a)` and every Borel
`C ⊆ 𝕐₂`, `R′(C | z⁽ⁿ⁾, a⁽ⁿ⁾) → R′(C | z, a)`. The restricted measure is not renormalized and may
have mass zero. -/
def ObsLawSetwiseContinuousOn
    (P : Kernel (X × A) X) [IsMarkovKernel P] (Q : Kernel (A × X) Y) [IsMarkovKernel Q]
    (Y₂ : Set Y) : Prop :=
  ∀ (z : ProbabilityMeasure X) (a : A) (zs : ℕ → ProbabilityMeasure X) (as : ℕ → A),
    Tendsto zs atTop (𝓝 z) → Tendsto as atTop (𝓝 a) →
      ∀ C : Set Y, MeasurableSet C → C ⊆ Y₂ →
        Tendsto (fun n => (obsLaw P Q (zs n) (as n) : Measure Y) C) atTop
          (𝓝 ((obsLaw P Q z a : Measure Y) C))

/-- Condition (c)(ii) of Theorem 7.1 (p. 25), Assumption (H) on `𝕐₂` for the filter `H`: whenever
`z⁽ⁿ⁾ → z` weakly and `a⁽ⁿ⁾ → a`, there are a subsequence `(z⁽ⁿᵏ⁾, a⁽ⁿᵏ⁾)` and a measurable
`C ⊆ 𝕐₂` with `R′(𝕐₂ ∖ C | z, a) = 0` such that `H(z⁽ⁿᵏ⁾, a⁽ⁿᵏ⁾, y) → H(z, a, y)` weakly for all
`y ∈ C`. -/
def FilterSubseqOn
    (P : Kernel (X × A) X) [IsMarkovKernel P] (Q : Kernel (A × X) Y) [IsMarkovKernel Q]
    (H : ProbabilityMeasure X → A → Y → ProbabilityMeasure X) (Y₂ : Set Y) : Prop :=
  ∀ (z : ProbabilityMeasure X) (a : A) (zs : ℕ → ProbabilityMeasure X) (as : ℕ → A),
    Tendsto zs atTop (𝓝 z) → Tendsto as atTop (𝓝 a) →
      ∃ φ : ℕ → ℕ, StrictMono φ ∧ ∃ C : Set Y, MeasurableSet C ∧ C ⊆ Y₂ ∧
        (obsLaw P Q z a : Measure Y) (Y₂ \ C) = 0 ∧
        ∀ y ∈ C, Tendsto (fun k => H (zs (φ k)) (as (φ k)) y) atTop (𝓝 (H z a y))

end Partition

end FeinbergPOMDP.WStar.Supplement


